  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nHigh pressure and a ridge tracking out of the region will provide \nfor warm and dry conditions today. Highs in the mid 70s to near 80 \nwith Td values in the upper 50 to around 60 will keep conditions \ncomfortable for the day. \n\nA warm front will track across the area on Thursday morning, \nushering in a warmer and more humid airmass within the warm sector \nof a sfc low tracking across Ontario and Quebec. Showers and \nthunderstorms will develop and move across the area, first with a \npre-frontal trough during the afternoon, and then again with an \nincoming cold front during the mid-evening hours. Most of the \nguidance brings around 1,500 J/kg of cape into the area. There still \nremains some uncertainty with the amount of clearing after the \npassage of the warm front and ahead of the incoming pre-frontal \ntrough. Shear values support damaging wind gusts with a lesser \nextent for hail; an isolated tornado can't be ruled out. Shear \nvalues during the afternoon/evening in the 30+ knot range are \nexpected and with increased clearing, cape values could reach 2,000+ \nJ/kg. For Thursday, a 'Slight Risk' is in place from SPC for all but \nthe far western portion of the BGM forecast area, where a 'Marginal \nRisk' for severe thunderstorms is in place. \n\nPWat values will increase to over 1.50 inches on Thursday, leading \nto the greater potential for thunderstorms to cause heavy rainfall \nand for flooding. A 'Marginal Risk' of excessive runoff is in place \nfor the entire area from WPC. A 'Slight Risk' is in place across the \nsoutheastern portion of the forecast area. \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nHigh pressure approaching and then crossing the region Friday into \nthe weekend will bring a round of mostly dry and fair weather. The \nonly caveat to this is a trough axis crossing the region on Friday \nmay bring a few quick passing showers. \n\nTemperatures will cool a few degrees on Friday and Saturday behind \nthe passing cold front on Thursday night, but warmer temperatures \nand increasing humidity will return for Sunday.",
